  <note>
    <content textType="body">
      <p>Documentation comes in three layers. The API contract is generated into Swagger UI from the controller annotations, so it cannot drift. The README tells you how to run the whole thing - compose profiles, curl examples, the simulator's rules. And SOLUTION.md is the layer I am most proud of: it records the design decisions and trade-offs, so a reviewer can see the reasoning rather than just the code. Documentation is not a page count; it is the absence of surprises.</p>
    </content>
  </note>
